t. That clause binds Session Event history, and Read classifies one completed CLI invocation rather than retaining any event, so this binding discharges none of Section 17.2's measured obligations. The four numbered reader rules the section states carry no RFC 2119 keyword and are therefore invisible to the clause scanner; three of them are implemented and tested here - Read and Decode settle the schema and major before any other member, the closed member set included, acceptsVersion implements the same-or-lower-minor rule, and an unknown namespaced extension survives a decode and re-encode byte for byte - while the unknown ownership/security enum rule is covered only for the closed CLI Result vocabularies, not for any lease or security enum, because no ownership implementation exists in this repository.\\\"\\ninternal/traceability/ownership.v0.5.0.json:2613:        \\\"section:17.4\\\"\\ninternal/traceability/ownership.v0.5.0.json:2624:      \\\"gap\\\": \\\"AssessCompatibility implements the Section 17.4 read-only downgrade assessment, but no clause of Section 17.4 is enumerated against an acceptance case.\\\"\\ninternal/traceability/ownership.v0.5.0.json:2731:      \\\"gap\\\": \\\"validateProviderIdentityRecord validates the Section 5.5 provider identity shape; the destination-adapter obligations of Section 5.5 are not implemented and no clause of it is enumerated.\\\"\\n===\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 3968,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 992,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
