{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c893","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06e59-f410-76d3-be05-ab6d05f2f618"},"sequence":676,"recorded_at":1780531400001347,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"1619d586-4e11-48b5-9a4b-4a908ec4863f","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"1619d586-4e11-48b5-9a4b-4a908ec4863f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"1619d586-4e11-48b5-9a4b-4a908ec4863f"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"3568dbce-4c89-4050-aa50-acf6c1c96f66"},"task_id":"3568dbce-4c89-4050-aa50-acf6c1c96f66","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"3568dbce-4c89-4050-aa50-acf6c1c96f66","chunk":"Read text file `README.md`.\n(69 line(s) above)\n70|DAG. It cannot block autonomous agent execution.\n71|\n72|See [.spec/README.md](.spec/README.md) for the pinned specification source,\n73|section coverage, board IDs, counts, and execution rules. Generated planning\n74|snapshots live in [.planning/](.planning/); the live task-board remains the\n75|planning authority.\n76|\n77|## Normative Source Pin\n78|\n79|[`internal/specpin`](internal/specpin) embeds one implementation lock for\n80|`agent-session-manager-spec@v0.5.0`. Its production `Current` and `Verify`\n81|entry points fail closed on a partial read, unknown member, source substitution,\n82|contract or fixture drift, and any byte-level lock change. It also projects the\n83|exact historical v0.4.3 registry without widening that immutable baseline.\n84|\n85|This package is read-only and does not mutate durable state. Repeated reads are\n86|idempotent and isolated from caller mutation. It deliberately adds no `ax`\n87|command, `doctor` result, conformance-target declaration, or runtime capability\n88|claim; those surfaces remain unavailable until their owning implementation and\n89|acceptance tasks land.\n90|\n91|## Pinned Specification Document\n92|\n93|[`internal/specdoc`](internal/specdoc) embeds the byte-exact `SPEC.md` of that\n94|same pinned release so repository fidelity gates can compare their artifacts\n95|against the specification text instead of against the implementation those\n96|artifacts are supposed to constrain. The upstream specification remains\n97|normative; this copy is a verification input and amends nothing.\n98|\n99|`Load` accepts the document only when its SHA-256 equals\n100|`specpin.DocumentSHA256`, so a substituted, edited, truncated, or unreadable\n101|document is refused rather than silently compared against — otherwise a swapped\n102|specification would confirm whatever it happened to contain. `QuoteLines`\n103|resolves an excerpt to the 1-based `SPEC.md` lines it begins on, `SectionID`\n104|resolves a line to the numbered clause that contains it, `TableRowAt` reports\n105|what a Markdown table body row declares, and all three work under one\n106|normalization rule: runs of ASCII whitespace collapse to a single space. Case,\n107|punctuation, digits, and inline `<code>` markup are compared exactly. A\n108|whitespace run that crosses a hard boundary collapses instead to a block\n109|separator that no normalized excerpt can contain, so a quote cannot stitch\n110|across one; both halves of such a stitch are individually verbatim, so\n111|whitespace collapsing alone admitted it. Two boundaries are hard: a blank line,\n112|which separates a block from the next, and the newline between two adjacent\n113|table rows, because a table row is a complete line by construction. Inside one\n114|block the newline is still forgiven, deliberately — the document's hard line\n115|wrapping, its table indentation, and the newline between two adjacent list items\n116|or two adjacent lines of one paragraph.\n117|\n118|Only repository gates import this package - the test binaries that check\n119|enumeration artifacts, and `internal/traceability`, which measures the clause\n120|inventory of a bound section from it. The embedded document never reaches the\n121|`ax` command, which does not exist yet, and\n122|`TestEmbeddedDocumentNeverReachesAProductBinary` is what keeps that true once it\n123|does: it reads the module import graph from source, refuses any `main` package\n124|outside `tracecheck` that can reach this package, and proves the detector by\n125|planting a `cmd/ax` that imports `internal/traceability`. It is read-only,\n126|mutates no durable state, and advertises no runtime capability.\n127|\n128|## Common Wire Scalar Types\n129|\n130|[`internal/scalar`](internal/scalar) implements the validated AX value types\n131|used by later schema owners: canonical lowercase UUIDv4 and UUIDv7 values, real\n132|UTC RFC3339 timestamps with millisecond-or-finer precision, SHA-256 digest\n133|identifiers, the current four-member AX platform vocabulary, bounded provider\n134|IDs, platform-neutral relative paths, platform-bound absolute paths, safe and\n135|bounded JSON integers, `decimal_uint64`, and exact lower-snake-case closed\n136|enums. Embedded Git values use the same production scalar layer for exact\n137|SHA-1/SHA-256 OIDs, fully qualified `git check-ref-format` references, and\n138|sanitized HTTPS/SSH/git remote URLs that contain no password or token, query,\n139|fragment, local path, or unsupported scheme.\n140|\n141|Timestamp validation accepts published UTC leap seconds, including\n142|`1990-12-31T23:59:60.000Z`, while refusing a fabricated `:60` in an ordinary\n143|minute or on an unpublished date. Because Go's `time.Time` has no leap-second\n144|representation, `Timestamp.Time` maps an accepted leap second to the following\n145|representable UTC second while the scalar retains the original wire text.\n146|\n147|Constructors and JSON/text decoders fail closed on malformed, null,\n148|out-of-range, wrong-version, traversal, encoded-separator, wrong-platform,\n149|unknown-enum, or fabricated leap-second inputs. `AbsolutePath` decoding\n150|requires the containing platform, and generic closed-enum decoding requires\n151|the exact negotiated vocabulary; neither guesses that context from a field\n152|name or value prefix. Native Windows paths additionally refuse Win32-reserved\n153|component punctuation, control characters, and DOS device names even when a\n154|device name has an extension; those Windows-only component rules do not alter\n155|POSIX path validation. These types are read-only value validation. They do not\n156|mutate durable state and add no `ax doctor` result, provider/platform\n157|availability claim, or runtime capability advertisement.\n158|\n159|`FuzzScalarProductionEntries` drives the production constructors and wire\n160|decoders with a checked-in corpus covering published and fabricated leap\n161|seconds, lowercase RFC3339, impossible dates, malformed identifiers, unsafe\n162|integer boundaries, and Windows reserved-device and wildcard components. Any\n163|accepted value must publish and read back byte-for-byte without a later\n164|refusal.\n165|\n166|Run the focused tests and assigned-scope gate with:\n167|\n168|```bash\n169|go test ./internal/scalar -count=1\n170|go test ./internal/scalar -cover -count=1\n171|go test ./internal/scalar -run=^$ \\\n172|  -fuzz=^FuzzScalarProductionEntries$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\n173|go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck\n174|```\n175|\n176|The assigned-scope gate refuses Sections 1.6, 10.1, 10.2, 10.3 and 10.4: each\n177|binding validates a corner of its section and the gate now says so with the\n178|measured ratio. See [Specification-to-Code Ownership\n179|Gate](#specification-to-code-ownership-gate).\n180|\n181|```bash\n182|go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck \\\n183|  -section 1.6 -section 10.1 -section 10.2 -section 10.3 -section 10.4\n184|# exits non-zero: 0/31, 0/3, 0/5, 1/3 and 0/25 normative clauses discharged\n185|```\n186|\n187|## Configuration Loading and Versioned Schemas\n188|\n189|The internal/config package implements the read-only Section 3.2 path-selection\n190|boundary used by Section 6.1 configuration loading. LoadOS captures the\n191|caller-supplied runtime-probed AX platform and current OS inputs once; Load is\n192|the dependency-injected production entry used by deterministic tests and\n193|alternate launchers.\n194|\n195|One five-row registry drives --config, --data-dir, --state-dir, --cache-dir,\n196|and --runtime-dir together with their exact AX_* counterparts. Resolution\n197|applies flag, non-empty documented environment override, then platform default\n198|independently to every path class. Relative flag and override values are made\n199|absolute against the captured working directory before use. XDG, macOS,\n(more lines below)"}}}
