{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d085","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06e59-f410-76d3-be05-ab6d05f2f618"},"sequence":1693,"recorded_at":1780531400003381,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"1619d586-4e11-48b5-9a4b-4a908ec4863f","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"1619d586-4e11-48b5-9a4b-4a908ec4863f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"1619d586-4e11-48b5-9a4b-4a908ec4863f"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"8c4a07d6-457c-4612-b968-3d62654e99db"},"task_id":"8c4a07d6-457c-4612-b968-3d62654e99db","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"8c4a07d6-457c-4612-b968-3d62654e99db","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 1-6\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-# Flight Logbook\n-\n-> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\n-> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\n-\n-## 2026-09-03\n+# Flight Logbook\n+\n+> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\n+> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\n+\n+## 2026-09-04\n+\n+### 0115 — Provider discovery leaf: the inventory gate caught a test proving nothing, and a trust test caught a double hash\n+\n+- SCOPE: new `internal/provider` (Discover/Trust/Verify over a filesystem seam), `README.md` section, TASK-260830-2890sd §7.1.\n+- FINDING: first full run was green except the new refusal-inventory gate, which named `provider.go:463` — the Verify re-read failure path. The `unreadable target` subtest set file content to nil without scripting a read error, so it exercised the digest-mismatch path while claiming the re-read path. Same class as entry 1447: a test passing while proving nothing about the path it names. Scripted `contentErr` fixed it; gate green.\n+- FINDING: `TestTrustRecordsCandidateFacts` caught a real double hash before commit — production called `sha256.Sum256` then `scalar.SHA256Digest` (which hashes again). Single `SHA256Digest(content)` now; Verify compares one hash against the receipt in constant time.\n+- DECISION: `ax-provider-<id>` names with an invalid suffix (e.g. `.bak`, uppercase) fail discovery with `invalid_config` rather than being skipped — a prefixed name signals intent and silent skipping would turn a typo'd install into a confusing absence. Bare non-prefixed entries are still ignored. Same-file-twice (two dirs, identical bytes) still fails: the section's MUST is unconditional and order confers no precedence.\n+- BOUND: native Windows owner attestation is unimplemented (`os_windows.go` refuses), so external executables are undiscoverable there; builtins unaffected. Package mutates no durable state — the host persists `TrustRecord`; no crash/idempotency surface inside. Ownership JSON untouched (hash-pinned; another scope's review owns it).\n+- EVIDENCE: `go test ./internal/provider/ -count=1` exit 0 (34 top-level PASS), cover 93.4%, `go vet`/`go build` clean, `GOOS=windows go build` clean, full `go test ./...` exit 0, tracecheck exit 0 unchanged at 17/403.\n+- STATUS: Resolved. TASK-260830-2890sd, handed to review.\n+\n+## 2026-09-03\n"}}}
