{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d281","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a06e59-f410-76d3-be05-ab6d05f2f618"},"sequence":1947,"recorded_at":1780531400003889,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"1619d586-4e11-48b5-9a4b-4a908ec4863f","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"1619d586-4e11-48b5-9a4b-4a908ec4863f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"1619d586-4e11-48b5-9a4b-4a908ec4863f"},"terminal":"completed","text":"TASK-260830-2890sd is ready for review (handed off to review, board status `to-review`, checklist 10/10).\n\nWhat was delivered:\n\n- New `internal/provider` package implementing SPEC §7.1 — production entry points `Discover`, `Trust`, `Verify` over an injectable filesystem seam with production `OSSystem`:\n  - Deterministic discovery in section order (plugin dirs listed order with bytewise-sorted entries, six built-ins in document order, PATH only when allowed).\n  - Trust recording (canonical path, SHA-256 digest, approving owner) and substitution detection — any changed target/digest/owner/shape or re-read failure fails with `integrity_failure`.\n  - Duplicate refusal with `invalid_config` naming both sources, structurally before any probe/execution (no probe/exec dependency; a duplicate fixture with a live script leaves its sentinel unexecuted).\n  - Fail-closed reads; codes pinned to the registry with exits 3/3/9.\n- Tests: 34 top-level PASS, 93.4% coverage, including specdoc-quoted §7.1 citations, an AST-derived refusal-inventory gate, and real-filesystem tests. The gate caught one unexercised path and a trust test caught a double-hash bug, both fixed pre-commit.\n- Evidence, all exit 0 and run directly: package tests + cover, `go vet`/`go build`, full `go test ./...`, `GOOS=windows` build, `tracecheck` unchanged at 17/403. Logs and outcome summary attached on the board.\n- Committed as signed `292fc6d`, one past checkpoint, worktree clean, nothing pushed.\n\nStated bounds: native Windows owner attestation unimplemented (externals undiscoverable there); same-file-twice still refuses; manifests/protocol/matrices belong to the sibling leaves.","reason":null}}
